From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:40:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: named temporary files without rustix

Repository: crates.io tempfile 3.20.0 (archive SHA-256 e8a64e39...d6a1)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: target_os = "aros"; other targets unchanged.
Upstream status: local-only (not submitted).
Problem: tempfile's Unix implementation uses rustix, which has no AROS
backend.
Change: the PdfCraft port's adapter (aros-artcraft pdfcraft,
patches/crates/tempfile-3.27.0) applied to 3.20.0: exclusive std opens for
named files; unnamed files and overwriting persist are refused.
Verification: Helix's save makes its backup with Builder::make_in and
keep; saving files on AROS One 1.3 (RAM:) works.
Removal: when rustix gains an AROS backend.
